---
import DocLayout from '../../layouts/DocLayout.astro';
import StatusBadge from '../../components/StatusBadge.astro';
import PermissionsTable from '../../components/PermissionsTable.astro';
import { channels } from '../../config/features';
import { facebookPermissions } from '../../config/permissions';

const toc = [
  { id: 'what', label: 'What the integration does' },
  { id: 'connect', label: 'How to connect' },
  { id: 'disconnect', label: 'How to disconnect' },
  { id: 'permissions', label: 'Permissions' },
  { id: 'data', label: 'How your data is handled' },
];
---

<DocLayout
  title="Facebook Messenger integration"
  description="How Get Assist connects to a Facebook Page to handle Messenger conversations, which permissions it asks for and why, and how to disconnect."
  toc={toc}
>
  <div slot="intro">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4">
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-semibold sm:text-5xl">Facebook Messenger integration</h1>
      <StatusBadge status={channels.facebook.status} />
    </div>
    <p class="mt-5 max-w-[60ch] text-xl leading-relaxed text-slate">
      Connect a Facebook Page so the messages people send it through Messenger arrive in your Get
      Assist inbox, where the AI and your team can answer them.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2 id="what">What the integration does</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Shows Messenger conversations sent to the Page you connect in your Get Assist inbox.</li>
    <li>
      Sends the replies that you, your teammates or the AI write back to the customer through
      Messenger.
    </li>
    <li>Lets the AI answer from your knowledge base and hand a conversation to your team.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Get Assist only works with the Pages you choose. It does not post to your Page, read your
    personal Facebook messages, or access Pages you did not select.
  </p>

  <h2 id="connect">How to connect</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Sign in to Get Assist and open the channel settings of your project.</li>
    <li>Choose to connect Facebook Messenger. You are taken to Facebook to log in.</li>
    <li>Review the permissions Facebook shows and choose the Page or Pages to connect.</li>
    <li>Return to Get Assist. New messages to that Page start appearing in your inbox.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>You need to be able to manage the Page in Facebook to connect it.</p>

  <h2 id="disconnect">How to disconnect or revoke access</h2>
  <p>You can stop Get Assist from accessing a Page in either of two ways:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>In Get Assist:</strong> open the channel settings of your project and disconnect the
      Page. New messages stop arriving straight away.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>In Facebook:</strong> open the settings for business integrations or apps connected to
      your account or Page, find Get Assist and remove it. This revokes the access you granted, even
      if you can no longer sign in to Get Assist.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    What happens to messages already stored after you disconnect is described on the{' '}
    <a href="/data-deletion">data deletion page</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="permissions">Permissions Get Assist asks for</h2>
  <PermissionsTable permissions={facebookPermissions} />

  <h2 id="data">How your data is handled</h2>
  <p>
    Get Assist uses the messages, sender names and attachments from your connected Page only to show
    conversations to your team, to generate suggested or automatic replies, and to send replies
    back. The <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> explains what is stored, who processes it and
    for how long.
  </p>
</DocLayout>
